Notebook[{
Cell["\<\
Build a Large Language Model from Scratch \[LongDash] in Wolfram Language\
\>", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"6e63b034-ccc7-447a-a6c9-36f6f9994fd1"],

Cell["\<\
A single-notebook walkthrough of the full pipeline, from byte-pair encoding \
to chat\
\>", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"c7dbe963-5f5f-4c08-8a8f-7084270aa83c"],

Cell["Companion repository \[Dash] all source, data and the trained chat model: https://github.com/mthiel74/LLM-A-to-Z-in-Wolfram . The code cells load one package, LLMAtoZ.wl, which is fetched automatically from GitHub if it is not sitting next to the notebook. To run and modify everything yourself, clone the repo and open this notebook from inside it \[Dash] every file path is then relative to the notebook's folder. Just reading? Every figure and output is already saved in the notebook.", "Text",
 FontWeight->"Bold",
 CellTags->"REPO-LINK"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook is a complete, self-contained tour of how to build a small but \
functional transformer-based language model entirely in Wolfram Language.  It \
walks every piece of the modern LLM stack \[LongDash] tokenisation, \
embeddings, attention, the transformer block, parameter accounting, \
pre-training, sampling, supervised fine-tuning, LoRA, classification, \
reinforcement learning, and an interactive chat widget \[LongDash] in one \
linear evaluation.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"699d2aef-eb2a-4b78-9b56-3af709a2ed02"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The final deliverable is a chat-style model you can actually talk ",
 "to inside Wolfram Desktop.  The whole pipeline runs on a Mac mini ",
 "in under a day of CPU time; a cloud path (",
 StyleBox["RemoteBatchSubmit",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ") is sketched for scaling up."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e1b20915-52d5-4dda-ba33-9e39e7502abf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The notebook is companion-in-spirit to Sebastian Raschka's ",
 StyleBox["Build a Large Language Model from Scratch",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " (Manning, 2024), and goes further into post-training territory ",
 "covered by Andrej Karpathy's ",
 StyleBox["nanochat",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " (2025).  Every line of code, every derivation, and the whole ",
 "exposition is original; the only overlap with the book is the ",
 "canonical mathematics of the transformer, which has been the same ",
 "since Vaswani et al. (2017)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2526832b-9ef3-4c37-831b-c5710e661e65"],

Cell["What you will build", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"b0f59a05-28dc-480a-b801-b92b08a5b238"],

Cell["\<\
Concretely, after evaluating this notebook end-to-end you will have on disk:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a6b0fa6d-1f23-4f3d-ac09-0b6a9af7036e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\[FilledSquare] A from-scratch byte-pair-encoding tokeniser learned ",
 "on Tiny Shakespeare (~4000 token vocabulary).\n",
 "\[FilledSquare] A character-level tokeniser (~65 symbol vocabulary) ",
 "for the small-model regime.\n",
 "\[FilledSquare] A configurable ",
 StyleBox["gptModel[d, h, L, dFF, V, n]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " constructor that builds the canonical pre-norm transformer at any ",
 "size from 1M parameters (toy) up to GPT-2 small at 124M parameters ",
 "(weight-tying enabled).\n",
 "\[FilledSquare] Two trained checkpoints: a 1.8M-parameter char-",
 "level model that produces Shakespeare-flavoured prose, and a ",
 "124M-parameter fine-tuned GPT-2 that speaks fluent conversational ",
 "English.\n",
 "\[FilledSquare] Five sampling strategies (greedy, temperature, ",
 "top-k, top-p, beam) and speculative decoding, all from scratch.\n",
 "\[FilledSquare] Three fine-tuning regimes (full SFT, LoRA, ",
 "classification head).\n",
 "\[FilledSquare] A GRPO-style RL post-training loop.\n",
 "\[FilledSquare] An interactive chat widget powered by the trained ",
 "model.\n",
 "\[FilledSquare] A working understanding of why every part of the ",
 "pipeline is the way it is."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8e12b3a1-0d01-4ce8-b60c-095295838d0c"],

Cell["The 30,000-foot view", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"b59adcb6-825d-4e1f-b018-c8da51a4d56b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 GraphicsBox[
  TagBox[RasterBox[CompressedData["1:"], {{0, 667.}, {1000., 0}}, {0, 255},
    ColorFunction->RGBColor,
    ImageResolution->{72, 72}],
   BoxForm`ImageTag[
   "Byte", ColorSpace -> "RGB", Interleaving -> True, 
    MetaInformation -> <|
     "Exif" -> <|
       "ImageWidth" -> 1000, "ImageLength" -> 667, "XResolution" -> 72, 
        "YResolution" -> 72, "ResolutionUnit" -> "Inch", "Software" -> 
        "Created with the Wolfram Language : www.wolfram.com", "DateTime" -> 
        DateObject[{2026, 5, 21, 15, 44, 25.}, "Instant", "Gregorian", 1.], 
        "TimeZoneOffset" -> 1|>|>],
   Selectable->False],
  DefaultBaseStyle->"ImageGraphics",
  ImageSizeRaw->{1000., 667.},
  PlotRange->{{0, 1000.}, {0, 667.}}]], "Output",
 CellMargins->{{Inherited, Inherited}, {5, 10}},
 TextAlignment->Center,
 CellLabel->"",ExpressionUUID->"eb41fff5-3902-4427-8d3a-52fd6b9c26db"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Figure 0.1.  The pipeline this notebook implements \
end-to-end: text becomes BPE tokens; tokens become integer IDs; two embedding \
layers turn IDs into vectors; a stack of transformer blocks processes the \
vectors; the head projects back to a probability distribution over the \
vocabulary.",
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic]], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"39469521-3a2c-48f3-adf9-\
6a60d0064fe5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every modern language model \[LongDash] GPT-2, Llama, Mistral, the ",
 "model you talk to in the wild \[LongDash] is fundamentally the same ",
 "function: a sequence of ",
 Cell[BoxData["n"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"ae9fe7f2-87f6-4f5c-8bf9-6e00dfd37dfa"],
 " integer token IDs goes in, a sequence of probability ",
 "distributions over a vocabulary of size ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"|", "V", "|"}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"0074c76d-aee2-4a12-a823-26a5df1a7bb3"],
 " comes out.  What changes between systems is the size of the ",
 "matrices and the training regime, not the shape of the function."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8a5d1668-1426-4717-b302-58936ac8fc13"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The notebook proceeds linearly through the pipeline above.  Each ",
 "section introduces one piece, derives whatever needs deriving, ",
 "implements it as a Wolfram Language ",
 StyleBox["NetGraph",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", and uses it.  By ",
 "the end of Chapter ",
 StyleBox["4",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " you have a model architecture; by Chapter ",
 StyleBox["5",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " you have a trained model that produces text; by Chapter ",
 StyleBox["7",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " you have a model that follows instructions and can be chatted ",
 "with from inside the notebook."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"59ba7772-7e10-4507-922f-c09477747f9a"],

Cell["Setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"dab7c52c-e341-42a2-82c8-0b3213906436"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The notebook expects to be opened from its repository directory; ",
 StyleBox["NotebookDirectory[]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " is used to anchor every file path.  No global PATH or environment ",
 "variable is required."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d7d7a352-3782-4831-8059-965051529686"],

Cell["If[StringQ[Quiet@NotebookDirectory[]], SetDirectory[NotebookDirectory[]]];  (* anchor relative paths (corpus, data) to this notebook's folder *)", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"6d4fac5f-869e-41c5-906f-102de49d0b97"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "All of the auxiliary functions used across the notebook live in a ",
 "single companion file, ",
 StyleBox["LLMAtoZ.wl",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", at the repo root.  Each chapter's helpers live in their own ",
 "context (",
 StyleBox["LLMAtoZ`Tokeniser`",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["LLMAtoZ`Attention`",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", \[Ellipsis], ",
 StyleBox["LLMAtoZ`Discussion`",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ") so you can tell which chapter a symbol comes from.  ",
 "If you'd rather see each chapter's source on its own, the file is ",
 "auto-generated from the per-part packages in ",
 StyleBox["part-NN/src/",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "; run ",
 StyleBox["wolframscript -file build_LLMAtoZ_wl.wls",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " to regenerate."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d7c3be01-42da-4f43-a275-56168faebe3a"],

Cell["Module[{local = Quiet@Check[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \"LLMAtoZ.wl\"}], $Failed]},\n  Get[If[StringQ[local] && FileExistsQ[local], local,\n    \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mthiel74/LLM-A-to-Z-in-Wolfram/main/LLMAtoZ.wl\"]]]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"8515a495-4299-4212-8deb-5afd24fa5452"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Load the corpus.  Tiny Shakespeare is a 1.1-megabyte concatenation ",
 "of public-domain Shakespeare play text, originally assembled by ",
 "Andrej Karpathy for ",
 StyleBox["char-rnn",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " (2015) and used as a benchmark across the literature ever since.  ",
 "It is small enough to train on, large enough that BPE produces a ",
 "non-trivial vocabulary, and out of copyright."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9139e488-2cd2-43d1-820e-52d1e2653fe5"],

Cell["\<\
text = Import[\"part-01-tokeniser-and-embeddings/data/tinyshakespeare.txt\", \
\"Text\"];
{StringLength[text], \"characters\"}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"a5e8e93b-4b93-4b33-8053-07009923f284"],

Cell["{1115393, characters}", "Output",
 FontFamily->"Courier",
 FontSize->12,
 CellLabel->"Out= ",ExpressionUUID->"6d9fe2dd-1c0e-42af-a9a2-1f465d971384"],

Cell["\<\
About 1.1 million characters.  About 250,000 whitespace-separated words.  65 \
distinct characters (upper- and lower-case letters, digits, punctuation, \
whitespace, newline).  Three numbers that will reappear throughout the \
notebook.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"92694dc4-8914-4553-9f9e-3ecbd33edb4f"],

Cell["A map of the whole notebook", "Subsection", CellTags -> "PART9-FLOWCHART"],

Cell["The notebook follows three paths to a working model. Path A trains the original GPT architecture on Tiny Shakespeare; Path B reuses OpenAI's pretrained GPT-2 weights for fine-tuning, RL, and the discussion model; Path C (Chapter 11, new) pretrains a model from scratch on cloud GPUs. The chart shows each model and the chapter where it is built.", "Text", CellTags -> "PART9-FLOWCHART"],

