Cell["1.  Tokenisation: turning text into integers", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"720c55a8-37ec-4eba-a4b6-5aedbf00a9d7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A language model does not see characters or words.  It sees ",
 "integers.  The tokeniser is the function that converts between the ",
 "two: a deterministic mapping ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"text", 
   RowBox[{" ", 
    RowBox[{"\[RightArrow]", " "}]}], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[DoubleStruckCapitalN]", "n"]}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"e6edccdd-fe0f-4832-874a-4e397aade1b8"],
 " sending text to a length-",
 Cell[BoxData["n"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"97f43be8-02e0-40b0-bf10-a8df5f069b74"],
 " sequence of integer IDs in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", "1", ",", " ", "\[Ellipsis]", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"|", "V", "|"}], "}"}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"f91d5a06-f4f5-435c-b051-246dc32fb616"],
 ", and back.  The choice of tokeniser is the choice of two numbers ",
 "that play against each other for the rest of the pipeline: the ",
 "vocabulary size ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"|", "V", "|"}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"2b482ca6-1ad1-47af-81ed-8633e73aa7fb"],
 " and the sequence length ",
 Cell[BoxData["n"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"92d2f41e-87ee-4a67-a307-78021dd92e9d"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0a653992-c9a9-42e6-8163-9abaa806ec61"],

Cell["1.1  Three slicing strategies", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"28d1c725-3cf8-480f-bb5e-4d18d0bf6d81"],

Cell["Three obvious tokenisation schemes bracket the design space.", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8407cee8-d1fd-4795-a40b-97f5cb14354a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Character-level. ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "Each character is its own token.  Tiny Shakespeare gives ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"|", "V", "|"}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"f9e6230e-5413-49eb-9fa8-ce45d66bacc6"],
 " = 65, ",
 Cell[BoxData["n"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"3aa05952-c50c-4fe7-917c-3d35724bef69"],
 " = 1.1 million.  Tiny vocabulary, gigantic sequence; the attention ",
 "block, which is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"O", "(", 
   SuperscriptBox["n", "2"], ")"}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"c4a1f070-7691-4b14-a290-9f7cbeb54dfd"],
 " expensive, spends almost all its compute on positional bookkeeping."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bf448a7e-8e2c-40a3-a7f5-9018414b3cd6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Word-level. ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "Each whitespace-separated word is its own token.  Tiny Shakespeare ",
 "gives ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"|", "V", "|"}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"4e70603a-a0b1-46cf-94dc-961750c2fdde"],
 " \[TildeEqual] 14,500, ",
 Cell[BoxData["n"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"026a6689-9108-4eec-b96e-e8c16c436409"],
 " \[TildeEqual] 252,000.  ",
 "Large vocabulary, manageable sequence; but every rare inflection ",
 "and proper noun gets a fresh ID the model sees once or twice in ",
 "training, and anything outside the vocabulary is an unrecoverable ",
 StyleBox["<UNK>",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a3631827-34b9-431a-a8cb-c3045d8c0e92"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Subword (BPE). ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "An interior point: learn a vocabulary by repeatedly merging the ",
 "most frequent adjacent pair of symbols.  Common short words ",
 "collapse to a single token; rare words decompose into a handful of ",
 "sub-word pieces; every input \[LongDash] including out-of-corpus ",
 "characters \[LongDash] is representable, because the base alphabet ",
 "of single characters always sits at the bottom of the merge tree.  ",
 "No ",
 StyleBox["<UNK>",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", ever.  ",
 "This is the algorithm GPT-2, GPT-3, Llama, and tiktoken all use."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7229dc45-382e-4d30-9d3e-b80a4ea15ccd"],

Cell["1.2  Byte-pair encoding, from first principles", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"b92c1a5b-e738-4eff-9963-d9b3033c1d68"],

Cell["\<\
BPE was originally a compression algorithm proposed by Philip Gage in 1994.  \
Its transplant to neural-network text tokenisation is by Sennrich, Haddow and \
Birch (ACL 2016).  The four-line algorithm:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7499cad6-6fb3-4208-84ab-90b6004937d6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["1.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " Start with the alphabet of base symbols (characters).\n",
 StyleBox["2.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " Across the pre-tokenised corpus, count every adjacent pair of symbols.\n",
 StyleBox["3.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " Treat the most frequent pair as a new symbol from now on; record the \
merge.\n",
 StyleBox["4.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " Repeat until the merge budget is spent."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"51e2e860-8700-4a64-9867-473f263d3051"],

Cell[BoxData[
 GraphicsBox[
  TagBox[RasterBox[CompressedData["1:"], {{0, 1000.}, {1000., 0}}, {0, 255},
    ColorFunction->RGBColor,
    ImageResolution->{72, 72}],
   BoxForm`ImageTag[
   "Byte", ColorSpace -> "RGB", Interleaving -> True, 
    MetaInformation -> <|
     "Exif" -> <|
       "ImageWidth" -> 1000, "ImageLength" -> 1000, "XResolution" -> 72, 
        "YResolution" -> 72, "ResolutionUnit" -> "Inch", "Software" -> 
        "Created with the Wolfram Language : www.wolfram.com", "DateTime" -> 
        DateObject[{2026, 5, 21, 15, 44, 26.}, "Instant", "Gregorian", 1.], 
        "TimeZoneOffset" -> 1|>|>],
   Selectable->False],
  DefaultBaseStyle->"ImageGraphics",
  ImageSizeRaw->{1000., 1000.},
  PlotRange->{{0, 1000.}, {0, 1000.}}]], "Output",
 CellMargins->{{Inherited, Inherited}, {5, 10}},
 TextAlignment->Center,
 CellLabel->"",ExpressionUUID->"c029f432-86ff-4b61-a8b4-65950edf2be4"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Figure 1.1.  A pre-token like \"speaking\" decomposes \
into a small number of sub-word pieces plus the end-of-word marker.",
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic]], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5cf3c989-3f8f-47c9-85fc-\
5309065f7909"],

