  ImageSizeRaw->{1000., 667.},
  PlotRange->{{0, 1000.}, {0, 667.}}]], "Output",
 CellMargins->{{Inherited, Inherited}, {5, 10}},
 TextAlignment->Center,
 CellLabel->"",ExpressionUUID->"52606c28-c466-4004-9831-b6e1d26c7016"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Figure 3.1.  The QKV picture.  Each input embedding \
is projected by three matrices into a query, a key, and a value.  The dot \
product of every query with every key gives the attention-score matrix.  The \
upper triangle is masked (causal).  Row-wise softmax produces the attention \
weights.  The weighted sum of the values is the output.",
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic]], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"adb4d436-c21e-4517-84fd-\
ff582a5572ce"],

Cell["\<\
Strip the fancy parts away.  Attention is the operation \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]each output token is a weighted sum of the input \
tokens, where the weights are learned from the input itself.\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]  Three lines:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a7dec8e0-071f-449a-9c7b-000bc6abaace"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\[FilledSmallCircle] Project each input vector three times by ",
 "three learned linear maps: a ",
 StyleBox["query ",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 Cell[BoxData["q"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"2458456e-4135-4168-9b1e-06c350ac1f5e"],
 ", a ",
 StyleBox["key ",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 Cell[BoxData["k"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"08f423ee-76ad-4cae-a1de-dbf4be6fea1f"],
 ", and a ",
 StyleBox["value ",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 Cell[BoxData["v"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"d06a0f15-39c0-47f1-865c-3f642f47037c"],
 ".\n",
 "\[FilledSmallCircle] For each position ",
 Cell[BoxData["i"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"b7ab8040-f2ff-4569-8b7e-67498cc74597"],
 ", compute the dot product of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["q", "i"]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"51972146-d1a9-4371-9850-a94b3ded02e9"],
 " with every ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["k", "j"]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"de3ab8ab-1a10-4d43-84fe-a58af2516f26"],
 " in the sequence.  Softmax these scores along ",
 Cell[BoxData["j"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"06b93de5-ccfa-4fe2-8bd5-725b561bd4de"],
 " to get attention weights summing to 1.\n",
 "\[FilledSmallCircle] The output at position ",
 Cell[BoxData["i"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"16eaad51-8451-40d1-a191-ec212b516d0a"],
 " is the weighted sum of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["v", "j"]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"c5e3d343-21e6-410b-b359-dab6a3e76c5b"],
 " using those weights."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e716fafe-ed44-40c1-9b34-2afa19e19b73"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Attention", "(", "Q", ",", " ", "K", ",", " ", "V", ")", 
  RowBox[{" ", 
   RowBox[{"=", " "}]}], "softmax", "(", 
  FractionBox[
   RowBox[{"Q", "\[CenterDot]", 
    SuperscriptBox["K", "\[Transpose]"]}], 
   SqrtBox[
    SubscriptBox["d", "k"]]], ")", "\[CenterDot]", "V"}]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontSize->15,ExpressionUUID->"5e66671e-ff72-400a-ba2d-1c45d0692180"],

Cell["3.1  Why divide by Sqrt[d_k]?", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"e7796baa-6a53-47f5-a554-19e1f19d7d45"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Most expositions assert the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FractionBox["1", 
   SqrtBox[
    SubscriptBox["d", "k"]]]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"103bbe11-7886-4bdc-ab01-d8212f44fafa"],
 " scaling factor.  We will derive it.  This derivation, along with ",
 "a few similar first-principles arguments later in this notebook, ",
 "is what separates a teaching post from a code dump."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d0d6ea08-ea40-4bb9-b0ac-987769f74343"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Suppose ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"q", ",", " ", "k", " ", "\[Element]", " ", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[DoubleStruckCapitalR]", 
    SubscriptBox["d", "k"]]}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"f8de9d0e-b774-47a9-8a20-59310a5e93dd"],
 " with each component independently drawn from a zero-mean ",
 "unit-variance distribution.  The dot product is a sum of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["d", "k"]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"6f56a13f-b649-42b2-9de6-4112f6f22b03"],
 " random terms ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["q", "i"], 
   SubscriptBox["k", "i"]}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"09fb96bb-949e-486d-b0b1-ecd8123e2bbf"],
 ".  Each term has mean 0 (since ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"E", "[", 
   SubscriptBox["q", "i"], 
   SubscriptBox["k", "i"], "]"}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"6722020d-e5a4-422e-8da0-1614dae753af"],
 " = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"E", "[", 
   SubscriptBox["q", "i"], "]", "\[CenterDot]", "E", "[", 
   SubscriptBox["k", "i"], "]"}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"2671b00a-25a6-4549-a58b-4b5dbaf7bd8b"],
 " = 0) and variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"E", "[", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    SubscriptBox["q", "i"], "2"], "]", "\[CenterDot]", "E", "[", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    SubscriptBox["k", "i"], "2"], "]"}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"d6fcc788-1bb1-4a1d-ac37-49206ed8ceb9"],
 " = 1.  By independence across ",
 Cell[BoxData["i"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"fce6357a-052a-4574-b2d2-4d8f407fc7d5"],
 ", the variance of the sum is the sum of the variances: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"Var", "(", "q", "\[CenterDot]", "k", ")", 
   RowBox[{" ", 
    RowBox[{"=", " "}]}], 
   SubscriptBox["d", "k"]}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"229b99a3-ee09-421c-922a-34e44fae3c6d"],
 ".  Standard deviation grows as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   SubscriptBox["d", "k"]]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"aef8b5fe-ef63-46c2-818b-9af3171fc214"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4aa223a5-13ed-4c05-86e3-ad2f51022932"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Verify empirically.  Sample 2000 Gaussian (q, k) pairs at three ",
 "values of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["d", "k"]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"60bc3042-475a-44b0-83f4-3c8d4188274e"],
 " and look at the dot-product distribution:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5ac44bc3-89e0-4a4f-b2e0-e2329da247f5"],

Cell["\<\
SeedRandom[1]; nSamples = 2000;
dks = {16, 64, 256};
dots = Association @ Table[
  d -> Table[
    With[{q = RandomReal[NormalDistribution[], d],
          k = RandomReal[NormalDistribution[], d]},
      q . k], {nSamples}], {d, dks}];
StandardDeviation /@ dots\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"fe39733a-0873-4273-a204-6136d424582b"],

Cell["<|16 -> 4.06888, 64 -> 7.9869, 256 -> 16.4231|>", "Output",
 FontFamily->"Courier",
 FontSize->12,
 CellLabel->"Out= ",ExpressionUUID->"16914527-0125-42b0-958a-37b4c066affa"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The empirical standard deviations come out to ~4, 8, 16 \[LongDash] exactly \
the predicted ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   SubscriptBox["d", "k"]]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"49532c9a-3702-4642-9656-6d40794c016d"],
 " of 4, 8, 16."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"159a89ba-3a4a-4479-b3c4-95d5e23e9a0d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 GraphicsBox[
  TagBox[RasterBox[CompressedData["1:"], {{0, 138.}, {500., 0}}, {0, 255},
    ColorFunction->RGBColor,
