 CellLabel->"",ExpressionUUID->"ffb5bdac-bccf-42eb-8d7c-b28a90e4a6de"],

Cell["Drop the embedder's output into it, get a same-shape output:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cb2718db-4da3-4de1-b336-5f8f233b7f9d"],

Cell["\<\
SeedRandom[42];
x = RandomReal[NormalDistribution[0, 0.1], {16, 64}];
out = head[x];
Dimensions[out]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"98c52e8c-c443-44ce-926d-db4b4ff55422"],

Cell["{1}", "Output",
 FontFamily->"Courier",
 FontSize->12,
 CellLabel->"Out= ",ExpressionUUID->"21140ae3-9cf7-4fb8-92d7-eb98ebedcf40"],

Cell["3.4  Multi-head attention", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"9ee05b11-561b-432b-b9b3-1e788934c08f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A single head can only attend in one way at a time.  Multi-head ",
 "attention runs ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["n", "heads"]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"5cdf865b-f97f-4b3c-aa72-748698a6efc2"],
 " parallel single-head computations: ",
 "each head applies its own learned projections of the full input ",
 "down to dimension ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["d", "head"]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"688106cd-2bd4-40c3-9207-e2e927714f3f"],
 ", computes attention independently, and produces a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["d", "head"]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"f9ca66d2-37ce-4461-9c8a-34847895db5a"],
 "-dimensional output.  The heads are concatenated and a final ",
 "linear projection mixes them back into a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["d", "model"]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"59ac0121-741b-404f-9664-fc5286d71215"],
 "-vector."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9683ee11-ad2a-420a-bd4a-206411521c87"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The architectural trick is to split ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["d", "model"]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"a26576a1-bcb2-432f-92de-914d6e3fbb81"],
 " into ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["n", "heads"]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"f9ee8447-b26c-4fdd-a12b-e3f6d9a03623"],
 " equal pieces so the multi-head version has the same parameter ",
 "count as a single-head version at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["d", "model"]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"18f84226-ac68-40dc-adf3-904f57985bad"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"82a63ec4-b192-4cce-b960-890a9e581ed6"],

Cell["\<\
mha = LLMAtoZ`Attention`multiHeadAttentionBlock[64, 4, 16];
mha[x] // Dimensions\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"dd6ee787-f8df-4d56-8b6f-ebb142d71e99"],

Cell["{16, 64}", "Output",
 FontFamily->"Courier",
 FontSize->12,
 CellLabel->"Out= ",ExpressionUUID->"c37a952b-79ff-4442-a2c1-3b578cf8dffc"],

Cell["3.5  What real attention looks like: GPT-2 small", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"9466f223-07fe-4ddb-8f74-7b9c0a40295d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We can do something the typical from-scratch tutorial cannot: load ",
 "a fully pretrained language model from ",
 StyleBox["NetModel",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " and look at its actual attention patterns.  GPT-2 small is a ",
 "12-layer transformer with 12 heads per layer at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["d", "model"]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"01d6a563-7016-4994-ab74-e1acc7606cd5"],
 " = 768.  Each block's attention sub-layer holds four learned ",
 "matrices: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["W", "Q"]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"69cf4f18-20fa-42a0-92bb-dd557eca1775"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["W", "K"]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"29ebf16d-bd3e-4ac0-a422-068c7d3c1bc8"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["W", "V"]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"db6dde67-1d8c-4f68-8554-b18d4d4ce38e"],
 " (768\[Times]768 each) plus an output projection.  We have the ",
 "weights; we can recompute the attention weight matrix by hand."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7e70d208-b156-4708-87ba-1b0806addc4a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 GraphicsBox[
  TagBox[RasterBox[CompressedData["1:"], {{0, 414.}, {500., 0}}, {0, 255},
    ColorFunction->RGBColor,
    ImageResolution->{144, 144}],
   BoxForm`ImageTag[
   "Byte", ColorSpace -> "RGB", Interleaving -> True, 
