 CellLabel->"",ExpressionUUID->"38d4161f-5e86-4f71-bbd4-938dad0280e8"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Figure 4.1.  One pre-norm transformer block: \
LayerNorm \[RightArrow] attention \[RightArrow] residual \[RightArrow] \
LayerNorm \[RightArrow] feed-forward \[RightArrow] residual.  Two sublayers, \
each in its own additive residual.  The residual stream is never normalised; \
only the input to each sublayer is.",
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic]], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"73d5fdd8-ca51-415f-827f-\
e232ec399ea1"],

Cell["4.1  Position-wise feed-forward", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"f3f5f501-6911-433c-be4e-e583de1e89a0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Attention lets every position look at every other position, but ",
 "within each position all it does is take a weighted average of ",
 "value vectors.  There is no per-position transformation that ",
 "mixes the features of a single token nonlinearly \[LongDash] no ",
 "place for the model to actually ",
 StyleBox["compute",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " on what it has gathered.  The feed-forward block is the model's ",
 "place to compute: a two-layer position-wise MLP with a non-",
 "linearity in the middle."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8a39b405-ec14-4139-a6de-b479005002f9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Conventionally ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["d", "ff"]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"20fea762-dfff-4dcb-9be8-64b929d00183"],
 " = 4 \[Times] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["d", "model"]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"4724de4e-6f6b-4cc6-99af-e9bd75718e6e"],
 " and the non-linearity is GELU.  This block is where most of the ",
 "transformer's parameter budget lives."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fa1a18a9-6a9e-4905-bd78-2d44038bac11"],

Cell["\<\
ffn = LLMAtoZ`Transformer`feedForwardBlock[64, 256, 16];
SeedRandom[1]; xx = RandomReal[NormalDistribution[0, 0.1], {16, 64}];
Dimensions[ffn[xx]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"abe40ef8-3541-4674-99ef-a6969014e5ca"],

Cell["{16, 64}", "Output",
 FontFamily->"Courier",
 FontSize->12,
 CellLabel->"Out= ",ExpressionUUID->"36e11836-eb33-41f1-8aed-d7ec75661ba7"],

Cell["4.2  Pre-norm vs post-norm", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"891c6667-39e3-4530-8714-8d69f12f1bf3"],

Cell["Two sub-layers, each in its own residual connection:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8bb1812c-fd76-4e54-985e-19f3803065cf"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"x", "'"}], 
  RowBox[{" ", 
   RowBox[{"=", " "}]}], "x", 
  RowBox[{" ", 
   RowBox[{"+", " "}]}], 
  RowBox[{"Attention", 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"LayerNorm", 
     RowBox[{"(", "x", ")"}]}], ")"}]}]}]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontSize->15,ExpressionUUID->"153fded6-6ad4-41d0-9b3a-aec3447f3553"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"y", 
  RowBox[{" ", 
   RowBox[{"=", " "}]}], 
  RowBox[{"x", "'"}], 
  RowBox[{" ", 
   RowBox[{"+", " "}]}], 
  RowBox[{"FFN", 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"LayerNorm", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"x", "'"}], ")"}]}], ")"}]}]}]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontSize->15,ExpressionUUID->"3c95a0b0-8b2b-4610-b005-dba27cc6d5b0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Two design choices visible here.  First, the LayerNorm sits ",
 StyleBox["before",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " each sub-layer, not after.  This is the ",
 StyleBox["pre-norm ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "ordering, which differs from the post-norm ordering of the ",
 "original Vaswani 2017 paper.  Second, each sub-layer is wrapped ",
 "in an additive residual."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"76bbe7df-fc20-4dda-a16d-f609d70374d9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Why pre-norm?  In a deep stack what matters is whether the ",
 "residual stream is ever destroyed.  Pre-norm normalises the ",
 StyleBox["input",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " to each sub-layer, then adds the sub-layer's output to the ",
 "unnormalised residual.  The residual stream is never normalised, ",
 "so a gradient flowing backward through ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["n", "layers"]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"ea7b3b9a-ac3a-4fc0-9f71-3d2b6bff6820"],
 " layers is the product of (1 + small_correction) factors \[LongDash] a \
well-behaved O(1) number.  Post-norm normalises ",
 StyleBox["after",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " the residual addition, so each layer rescales the residual ",
 "stream by 1/std, and the backward gradient is a product of ",
 "repeatedly-rescaled numbers, which can compress to zero quickly."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1cfad845-6aa5-4ea5-8414-ea8e0d2729e5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 GraphicsBox[
  TagBox[RasterBox[CompressedData["1:"], {{0, 277.5}, {500., 0}}, {0, 255},
    ColorFunction->RGBColor,
    ImageResolution->{144, 144}],
   BoxForm`ImageTag[
   "Byte", ColorSpace -> "RGB", Interleaving -> True, 
    MetaInformation -> <|
     "Exif" -> <|
       "ImageWidth" -> 1000, "ImageLength" -> 555, "XResolution" -> 144, 
        "YResolution" -> 144, "ResolutionUnit" -> "Inch", "Software" -> 
        "Created with the Wolfram Language : www.wolfram.com", "DateTime" -> 
        DateObject[{2026, 5, 21, 15, 44, 38.}, "Instant", "Gregorian", 1.], 
        "TimeZoneOffset" -> 1|>|>],
   Selectable->False],
  DefaultBaseStyle->"ImageGraphics",
  ImageSizeRaw->{500., 277.5},
  PlotRange->{{0, 500.}, {0, 277.5}}]], "Output",
 CellMargins->{{Inherited, Inherited}, {5, 10}},
 TextAlignment->Center,
 CellLabel->"",ExpressionUUID->"c9d3989d-015e-4175-a9e4-f375bbd52c86"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Figure 4.2.  Forward-pass activation-norm growth on a \
randomly-initialised stack.  Pre-norm grows linearly with depth; post-norm \
flattens (the LayerNorm at the end of every block pins the magnitude to 1).  \
The reverse pattern in backprop is what makes post-norm hard to train at \
depth without warmup tricks.  GPT-2/3, LLaMA, Mistral, nanochat all use \
pre-norm.",
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic]], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"850f9699-46e6-4225-9711-\
aadd1880c46f"],

Cell["\<\
block = LLMAtoZ`Transformer`transformerBlock[64, 4, 256, 16];
{block[xx] // Dimensions, Information[block, \"ArraysTotalElementCount\"]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"01c8101b-7d2a-43ca-848e-7a023b9983a2"],

Cell["{{16, 64}, 50560}", "Output",
 FontFamily->"Courier",
 FontSize->12,
 CellLabel->"Out= ",ExpressionUUID->"21e33f4e-a04d-44df-ac42-8d10f6607125"],

Cell["4.3  Stacking + the full GPT model", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"0370b149-b770-49c3-83d9-67f1bf633720"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Stack ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["n", "layers"]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"7a5dedad-1e6f-495b-b3dc-314f2ab4ce67"],
 " of these blocks, prepend an embedder, append a final LayerNorm ",
 "and an output projection of shape (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["d", "model"]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"ed7c180f-59b3-45e9-ae0e-ac7627586352"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"|", "V", "|"}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"eda10847-1c23-4864-b884-4767f35036f5"],
 "), and you have a complete GPT-style language model."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"67dfd060-6257-4ff4-8cad-82bae298b8b6"],

Cell["\<\
model = LLMAtoZ`Transformer`gptModel[256, 8, 6, 1024, 1064, 256];
demoIds = RandomInteger[{1, 1064}, 256];
Dimensions[model[demoIds]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"a2ba07b8-2a85-4c3b-8bc0-e687c488afdf"],

Cell["{256, 1064}", "Output",
 FontFamily->"Courier",
 FontSize->12,
 CellLabel->"Out= ",ExpressionUUID->"0d76ab08-10d6-4a03-b7e9-808916201a07"],

Cell["\<\
(seqLen, |V|) out, as advertised.  Every row of the output is the pre-softmax \
logit vector at one position.  During training we shift by one and ask the \
model to predict the next token.  During inference we apply softmax to the \
last row and sample.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0cee82f7-bfb8-447a-aecb-ac424b4980d0"],

Cell["4.4  Counting parameters", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"396d8e13-65f4-490d-a51a-e41379efe749"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A pre-norm transformer block of size (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["d", "model"]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"19c61aa9-ec15-4b15-a07b-f5adb6ef1528"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["d", "ff"]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"24c71295-be50-46b5-a48d-9d21c3ffdbf9"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["n", "heads"]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"5c9525d6-2219-4462-a144-8005381b66cd"],
 ") has, in closed form:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2427821e-354e-4f43-ad97-9ed362377371"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\[FilledSmallCircle] Q, K, V projections summed over heads: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"3", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    SubscriptBox["d", "model"], "2"]}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"46937590-0d29-4e47-b1ed-017325791106"],
 ".\n",
 "\[FilledSmallCircle] Output projection: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   SubscriptBox["d", "model"], "2"]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"d76f8fc9-2471-4651-b4d3-b6582288b147"],
 ".\n",
 "\[FilledSmallCircle] Two LayerNorms (scale + bias each): ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", 
   SubscriptBox["d", "model"]}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"b17aebdb-423a-4e64-a1a6-3319b6aa5004"],
 ".\n",
 "\[FilledSmallCircle] FFN linears (with biases): ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   SubscriptBox["d", "model"], 
   SubscriptBox["d", "ff"], 
   RowBox[{" ", 
    RowBox[{"+", " "}]}], 
   SubscriptBox["d", "ff"], 
   RowBox[{" ", 
    RowBox[{"+", " "}]}], 
   SubscriptBox["d", "model"]}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"10c7f2f9-1697-4958-bf01-9b5dc3cf1d77"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1e459ef8-0bce-4d6e-b80e-eb14363aa722"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  SubscriptBox["params", "block"], 
  RowBox[{" ", 
   RowBox[{"=", " "}]}], "4", 
  SuperscriptBox[
   SubscriptBox["d", "model"], "2"], 
  RowBox[{" ", 
   RowBox[{"+", " "}]}], "2", 
  SubscriptBox["d", "model"], 
  SubscriptBox["d", "ff"], 
  RowBox[{" ", 
   RowBox[{"+", " "}]}], 
  SubscriptBox["d", "ff"], 
  RowBox[{" ", 
   RowBox[{"+", " "}]}], "5", 
  SubscriptBox["d", "model"]}]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontSize->15,ExpressionUUID->"29ab18e0-8cd7-47ac-a152-a5819819d70f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "On top of the blocks: embeddings (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["d", "model"], "(", 
   RowBox[{"|", "V", "|"}], 
   RowBox[{" ", 
    RowBox[{"+", " "}]}], 
   SubscriptBox["n", "max"], ")"}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"c88f2be1-da45-405e-b532-1e1ca5c1f5f4"],
 "), a final LayerNorm (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   SubscriptBox["d", "model"]}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"d88a074f-6127-463c-a309-1631437a9d45"],
 "), and an output projection (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["d", "model"], 
   RowBox[{"|", "V", "|"}]}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"3eaaa72b-550e-4e80-b4bc-9367ac99f748"],
 "; can be tied to the input embedding to save these parameters).  ",
 StyleBox["parameterCount[spec]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " computes the closed form; ",
 StyleBox["parameterCountFull[spec]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " adds the frozen causal-mask arrays we bake into each attention ",
 "head (one ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["n", "heads"]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"6ff24425-f6c4-455c-a377-67c4150c9462"],
 " \[Times] (maxSeqLen)\[Times](maxSeqLen) tensor per layer)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9269f6db-008b-4b6b-8d20-f0fcf582dc9c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 GraphicsBox[
  TagBox[RasterBox[CompressedData["1:"], {{0, 381.5}, {500., 0}}, {0, 255},
    ColorFunction->RGBColor,
