Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Figure 4.3.  Where the parameters go in our reference \
5M-parameter model.  Most of the trainable parameters (37%) live in the FFN; \
the frozen causal masks contribute another 37% of the array count even though \
they are not trainable.  Attention QKV projections are 14%.  Embedding tables \
and LayerNorms together are < 5%.",
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic]], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cce64bda-15b3-44cd-9524-\
6f26ef4ee0c1"],

Cell["4.5  Reconstructing GPT-2", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"ee62119e-5bb4-4bbd-a5ad-9ee8102b1ee5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A natural test of our ",
 StyleBox["gptModel",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " constructor: can it build GPT-2 small?  Plug in the architectural ",
 "spec and the parameter formula should give ~124M with weight ",
 "tying enabled (sharing the input embedding with the output ",
 "projection)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d1e55bdf-c851-4053-ad45-83d4857ad177"],

Cell["\<\
gpt2Spec = LLMAtoZ`Transformer`gpt2SmallSpec[];
{LLMAtoZ`Transformer`parameterCount[gpt2Spec],
 LLMAtoZ`Transformer`parameterCount[gpt2Spec, \"WeightTying\" -> True]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"d296264b-d196-406f-8eb8-483249644641"],

Cell["{163050577, 124453201}", "Output",
 FontFamily->"Courier",
 FontSize->12,
 CellLabel->"Out= ",ExpressionUUID->"eba29108-ba44-49a2-84ea-fe65cc1eae85"],

Cell["\<\
Without weight tying: 163M.  With weight tying: 124,453,201 \[LongDash] \
matching real GPT-2 small (124,439,808) to within 13,000 parameters, a < \
0.01% discrepancy from minor LayerNorm-bias conventions.  The architecture \
itself is the same.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ae8f9507-6fc8-400f-8d1f-92423083367a"],

Cell["\<\
Two equivalent ways forward exist for the rest of the notebook:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5f3ffdf7-d527-4e2f-ab01-6fe2c116313d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\[FilledCircle] ",
 StyleBox["Build from scratch:",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " ",
 StyleBox["buildGpt2Architecture[\"Small\"]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " constructs an empty 124M net at GPT-2's spec; we train it from ",
 "random init.  Infeasible on Mac mini CPU.\n",
 "\[FilledCircle] ",
 StyleBox["Load the pretrained NetModel:",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " ",
 StyleBox["loadPrebuiltGpt2[]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " returns OpenAI's trained checkpoint (498 MB on first download).  ",
 "We skip pretraining and fine-tune from real weights.  This is what ",
 "Path A in Chapter 7 below uses."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5349e8d6-6a4e-49a6-a392-5877797bf594"],

Cell["5.  Pre-training: actually training a model", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"d16af0fa-c60b-4026-91cf-ab3bcf03b953"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Up to here, every model we have built has been randomly ",
 "initialised.  Time to train one.  The training task is next-token ",
 "prediction: each (input, target) pair is a context window and the ",
 "same window shifted one step forward.  Cross-entropy loss against ",
 "the shifted targets is what ",
 StyleBox["NetTrain",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " optimises."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"27537c28-08a5-43cd-a620-b4f844c2466f"],

Cell["5.1  The training loop, in one call", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"d1ca7623-2778-4106-887e-60820feb7588"],

Cell["\<\
After three chapters of careful construction, the training loop is wrapped in \
one function:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f7121090-382c-475c-a537-b5aa8872d5a6"],

Cell["\<\
(* SKIP: heavy training; the trained checkpoints already exist on disk *)
(* tinyResult = LLMAtoZ`Training`trainGptModel[
     <|\"label\" -> \"tiny\", \"dModel\" -> 96, \"nHeads\" -> 4,
       \"nLayers\" -> 3, \"dFF\" -> 256,
       \"vocabSize\" -> Length[vocab], \"maxSeqLen\" -> 64|>,
     ids, <|\"BaseLR\" -> 0.002, \"MaxRounds\" -> 3|>]; *)
\"checkpoint at part-04-pretraining/data/tiny_gpt_trained.wlnet\"\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"77dcb8d0-97e1-46c9-ac06-f7a67d24949a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Internally ",
 StyleBox["trainGptModel",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " does what every transformer training loop does:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e183472b-1186-48ae-82da-f1e11c5f3085"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "1. Slide a length-",
 Cell[BoxData["L"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"3083d425-3bcf-42c0-a7c0-269b2faa82dd"],
 " window through the token stream to produce (input, target) pairs.\n",
 "2. Build the model at the given spec via ",
 StyleBox["gptModel",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ".\n",
 "3. Wrap with a final softmax (see Section 5.3 for why).\n",
 "4. Hand it all to ",
 StyleBox["NetTrain",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " with ",
 StyleBox["CrossEntropyLossLayer",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", ADAM, a batch size, a learning-rate schedule, and a ",
 StyleBox["MaxTrainingRounds",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " cap.\n",
 "5. Return the trained net plus its per-round loss history."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fdb9963b-c50a-4a41-a019-8249f3fd1a95"],

Cell["5.2  The cosine LR schedule", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"f160cb2e-24ad-4424-aff4-cd2cfab9dc3f"],

Cell["\<\
The first ~10% of training linearly ramps the learning rate up to its peak; \
the remaining 90% cosine-decays it to 10% of peak.  Warmup avoids first-batch \
instability; cosine decay avoids late-training noise when the loss landscape \
flattens.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"69b7d5ea-9690-414f-adfa-84ace1460d38"],

Cell["\<\
Plot[LLMAtoZ`Training`cosineSchedule[r, 100, 0.001, 0.1],
  {r, 0, 100}, Frame -> True,
  FrameLabel -> {\"round (% of total)\", \"learning rate\"},
  PlotLabel -> \"Linear warmup (10%) + cosine decay\",
  PlotStyle -> Directive[ColorData[97][2], Thick], ImageSize -> 640]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"7b772fd5-3ecc-4e8e-b450-9447e5a4bd09"],

Cell[BoxData[
 GraphicsBox[
  TagBox[RasterBox[CompressedData["1:"], {{0, 460.8}, {720., 0}}, {0, 255},
    ColorFunction->RGBColor,
    ImageResolution->{100, 100}],
   BoxForm`ImageTag[
   "Byte", ColorSpace -> "RGB", Interleaving -> True, 
    MetaInformation -> <|
     "Exif" -> <|
       "ImageWidth" -> 1000, "ImageLength" -> 640, "XResolution" -> 100, 
        "YResolution" -> 100, "ResolutionUnit" -> "Inch", "Software" -> 
        "Created with the Wolfram Language : www.wolfram.com", "DateTime" -> 
        DateObject[{2026, 5, 21, 15, 44, 55.}, "Instant", "Gregorian", 1.], 
        "TimeZoneOffset" -> 1|>|>],
   Selectable->False],
  DefaultBaseStyle->"ImageGraphics",
  ImageSizeRaw->{720., 460.8},
  PlotRange->{{0, 720.}, {0, 460.8}}]], "Output",
 CellMargins->{{Inherited, Inherited}, {5, 10}},
 TextAlignment->Center,
 CellLabel->"",ExpressionUUID->"5368a861-c5c8-4e54-a3f4-48355a461814"],

Cell["5.3  A bug worth sharing: the missing softmax", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"f39611e1-3e20-468f-a630-2299f2751e65"],

Cell[BoxData[
 GraphicsBox[
  TagBox[RasterBox[CompressedData["1:"], {{0, 667.}, {1000., 0}}, {0, 255},
    ColorFunction->RGBColor,
    ImageResolution->{72, 72}],
   BoxForm`ImageTag[
   "Byte", ColorSpace -> "RGB", Interleaving -> True, 
    MetaInformation -> <|
     "Exif" -> <|
       "ImageWidth" -> 1000, "ImageLength" -> 667, "XResolution" -> 72, 
        "YResolution" -> 72, "ResolutionUnit" -> "Inch", "Software" -> 
        "Created with the Wolfram Language : www.wolfram.com", "DateTime" -> 
        DateObject[{2026, 5, 21, 15, 44, 55.}, "Instant", "Gregorian", 1.], 
        "TimeZoneOffset" -> 1|>|>],
   Selectable->False],
  DefaultBaseStyle->"ImageGraphics",
  ImageSizeRaw->{1000., 667.},
  PlotRange->{{0, 1000.}, {0, 667.}}]], "Output",
 CellMargins->{{Inherited, Inherited}, {5, 10}},
 TextAlignment->Center,
 CellLabel->"",ExpressionUUID->"6ab3bb96-4868-489d-83f5-85a9d1917959"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Figure 5.1.  The signature of the bug, side-by-side.  \
Left: cross-entropy without a softmax wrap descends past zero into \
unbounded-negative territory \[LongDash] not training, just driving one logit \
to +infinity to game an unbounded loss.  Right: with the softmax wrap, proper \
non-negative cross-entropy descends from log(|V|) to a positive asymptote.",
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic]], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"764d646e-2509-4b7d-91ca-\
d143d183ae55"],

Cell["\<\
This section earns its place because it captures a class of silent error that \
the series has the right tooling to surface, and because it tripped us up \
during development.  The naive way to define the loss is\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a122a30f-911d-4376-ab55-110bce2067e6"],

Cell["\<\
(* DON'T do this with raw logits *)
(*  NetTrain[..., LossFunction -> CrossEntropyLossLayer[\"Index\"]]  *)\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"b69afd13-ac2b-43f8-8509-b011069a8d3d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["CrossEntropyLossLayer[\"Index\"]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " expects ",
 StyleBox["probabilities",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " as input and computes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"-", "log"}], 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"p", "[", "target", "]"}], ")"}]}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"4a7a15f9-3eda-47b6-a50f-a2220a90bdb5"],
 " \[LongDash] non-negative by construction.  Our ",
 StyleBox["gptModel",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " emits raw logits.  Feed logits straight into ",
 StyleBox["CrossEntropyLossLayer[\"Index\"]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " and the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]loss\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] becomes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"-", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"logit", "[", "target", "]"}], ")"}]}], "+", "constant"}]], 
  "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"a8a9d63a-6002-452e-919a-7b3547b4529d"],
 ", which is unbounded below."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5bec7087-6064-4012-954a-77db03dfae22"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For BPE vocab ~4000 this happened to be okay: the optimiser ",
 "couldn't drive a single logit unbounded without similarly moving ",
 "all the others through the shared linear projection, and the ",
 "training landed in regimes that produced sensible token ",
 "distributions.  For a 65-character vocabulary, no such constraint ",
 "applied: the first overnight char-level run, after 6.5 hours, ",
 "produced a model whose maximum logit was ",
 StyleBox["+9,415",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " and whose generations were the single character ",
 StyleBox["'s'",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " repeated to fill the buffer."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a15a05af-024c-437d-bfbf-0b6bcad1de71"],

Cell[BoxData[
 GraphicsBox[
  TagBox[RasterBox[CompressedData["1:"], {{0, 325.}, {500., 0}}, {0, 255},
    ColorFunction->RGBColor,
    ImageResolution->{144, 144}],
   BoxForm`ImageTag[
   "Byte", ColorSpace -> "RGB", Interleaving -> True, 
    MetaInformation -> <|
     "Exif" -> <|
       "ImageWidth" -> 1000, "ImageLength" -> 650, "XResolution" -> 144, 
        "YResolution" -> 144, "ResolutionUnit" -> "Inch", "Software" -> 
        "Created with the Wolfram Language : www.wolfram.com", "DateTime" -> 
        DateObject[{2026, 5, 21, 15, 44, 55.}, "Instant", "Gregorian", 1.], 
        "TimeZoneOffset" -> 1|>|>],
   Selectable->False],
  DefaultBaseStyle->"ImageGraphics",
  ImageSizeRaw->{500., 325.},
  PlotRange->{{0, 500.}, {0, 325.}}]], "Output",
 CellMargins->{{Inherited, Inherited}, {5, 10}},
 TextAlignment->Center,
 CellLabel->"",ExpressionUUID->"0b5e1b34-211c-46df-bddf-ebf40646e76e"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Figure 5.2.  The broken loss curve, descending \
smoothly past zero into -10.  Preserved as a teaching artefact.",
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic]], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"816c9374-6dc9-4a71-bdcf-\
01dafcadf07c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A cross-entropy loss curve that descends ",
 StyleBox["below zero",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " is the signature.  Cross-entropy is bounded below by zero.  A ",
 "loss going negative is not \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]training is ",
 "going great\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]; it is \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]",
 "you are not optimising what you think you are.\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d84067f6-7938-4fe3-b55e-c2e04352860d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The fix is one line: wrap the model in ",
 StyleBox["NetMapOperator[SoftmaxLayer[]]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " before training, strip after.  ",
 StyleBox["trainGptModel",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " in the package now does this automatically."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f769b4b4-3bb4-4e4b-91d5-7276752ca1c1"],

Cell["5.4  Watching the model dream up Shakespeare", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"bb5ce9a8-08d5-4cd7-a0e5-b2c75ab7c8e1"],

Cell["\<\
We ran the corrected training for 5.5 hours on a Mac mini.  A background \
watchdog snapshot generations every time a new round completed.  Below: every \
round of training, the loss, the perplexity, and 200-character generations \
from two prompts at temperature 0.8.  Watch the output evolve from noise to \
Shakespeare-flavoured prose.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"eecbdbfc-efbe-4c58-82b1-c2d201448fdb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Round 7",
  FontSize->13,
  FontWeight->Bold,
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.4, 0.2, 0.5]],
 "  \[Bullet]  loss = ",
 "1.270",
 "  \[Bullet]  perplexity = ",
 "3.56",
 "  \[Bullet]  wall = ",
 "60.2",
 " min"
}], "Subsubsection",ExpressionUUID->"0e378db3-cd40-4c70-ae97-f4abc153c598"],

Cell["\<\
ROMEO:
You shall attard you: but she advise you, pretty,
And be as immediation'd and art that said
At the greater, thou hast privateless sons,
Thy son, the king with the singlition,
Whose cruels shop her pa\
\>", "Program",
 FontFamily->"Courier",
 FontSize->11,ExpressionUUID->"0d9db2c0-54ed-43e2-9c91-2585c754dc6f"],

Cell["\<\
HAMLET:
He knows will stay, we stars his foot
And heart a visage.

LEONTES:
Come;
I have not read with his soul.

PAULINA:
Good flesh are dead.

PETRUCHIO:
Ah, beliver, some stread my noble loar.

KATHARINA:
\
\>", "Program",
 FontFamily->"Courier",
 FontSize->11,ExpressionUUID->"563b0e9b-c984-4076-906f-583f03dbb427"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Round 8",
  FontSize->13,
  FontWeight->Bold,
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.4, 0.2, 0.5]],
 "  \[Bullet]  loss = ",
 "1.236",
 "  \[Bullet]  perplexity = ",
 "3.44",
 "  \[Bullet]  wall = ",
 "65.2",
 " min"
}], "Subsubsection",ExpressionUUID->"d1b2a7f6-670d-483a-8d4b-c84ea99aa726"],

Cell["\<\
ROMEO:
The love horry that shall pluck these consums!
And let me length the cursting the crown.

LUCENTIO:
I will not cheerful; and the senators and not the
sea to the daughter of this fortune to make thee,\
\>", "Program",
 FontFamily->"Courier",
 FontSize->11,ExpressionUUID->"9bc1e827-d1c1-4580-832a-fa1d2bfbdce7"],

Cell["\<\
HAMLET:
Good boy, you gave me, sir! and But what, you shall be
fellow not able?

ANGELO:
Good Good Montague as the thy deeds of
From chaptise I thy live:

ISABELLA:
Good trumpeth!

FLORIZEL:
I know how thou, \
\>", "Program",
 FontFamily->"Courier",
 FontSize->11,ExpressionUUID->"59bdb818-1a5c-4d6d-87d0-1d2dcb7c3af4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Round 9",
  FontSize->13,
  FontWeight->Bold,
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.4, 0.2, 0.5]],
 "  \[Bullet]  loss = ",
 "1.204",
 "  \[Bullet]  perplexity = ",
 "3.33",
 "  \[Bullet]  wall = ",
