Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Figure 7.2.  LoRA decomposition.  The frozen \
pretrained weight W is left alone; two small matrices A (8x768) and B (768x8) \
are added.  Effective weight: W + B.A.  Trainable parameters: 12K vs 589K, a \
48-fold reduction.",
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic]], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5f1c8452-28a8-4e25-a0b5-\
a12ace4a6d7e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Full SFT updates every weight in the pretrained model.  ",
 StyleBox["LoRA",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " (Hu et al. 2021) updates a tiny fraction.  For each linear ",
 "layer with weight ",
 Cell[BoxData["W"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"b6c539a9-09dd-47a6-a573-94a1fcbf3a21"],
 " of shape ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["d", "in"], "\[Times]", 
   SubscriptBox["d", "out"]}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"11b8615c-a3bd-4846-a8c6-06c581a09de6"],
 ", freeze ",
 Cell[BoxData["W"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"bb812e36-f2b2-4489-a261-6a1dcb2d378c"],
 " and learn two small matrices ",
 Cell[BoxData["A"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"91ed0703-3b53-41b0-9af3-19d9002f9edd"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["B"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"dfef8902-a92b-4ea9-9363-0190253a3624"],
 " of rank ",
 Cell[BoxData["r"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"fcfff13a-69f2-44fc-a74d-a337364ed3ce"],
 " so the effective weight at inference is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"W", "+", "BA"}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"7592f7ee-c9cb-4af2-9104-b192a6bb68b3"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0f20beae-1d2f-48ca-b84f-12c883cd5d15"],

Cell["\<\
LLMAtoZ`Lora`loraParameterCount[768, 768, #] & /@ {4, 8, 16, 32, 64}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"7aa92630-0bc2-49c7-abf0-428f5fc85a64"],

Cell["{6144, 12288, 24576, 49152, 98304}", "Output",
 FontFamily->"Courier",
 FontSize->12,
 CellLabel->"Out= ",ExpressionUUID->"08febfdc-a445-4c32-9d18-b86fa0703da1"],

Cell["\<\
12K LoRA parameters per 768\[Times]768 layer at rank 8 versus 590K for full \
fine-tuning.  48\[Times] reduction per layer; with 12 layers and four \
LoRA-wrapped projections per block (Q, K, V, O), the total trainable \
parameter count drops to ~1.2M vs 28M for full SFT.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fdadc4d4-ec5a-4141-987c-e42aa6308dfe"],

Cell["7.4  Classification fine-tuning (Raschka chapter 6)", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"b167f8c9-f5b2-4d15-8d1b-e89d4e8cf2c3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Same pretrained model, different task.  Strip the LM head, pool ",
 "the last-position hidden state with a ",
 StyleBox["SequenceLastLayer",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", project to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["n", "classes"]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"8e7542a5-7f8c-42bc-9c3d-226f7130d89f"],
 " logits.  ",
 "The rest of the pretrained backbone is reused as-is."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"05024e88-51a2-42b7-a1f9-514652506364"],

Cell["\<\
(* Demo: classify Shakespeare excerpts as tragedy vs comedy *)
LLMAtoZ`Classification`shakespeareGenreLabels[][[1 ;; 4]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"cbf01e0b-f7bb-4af5-85d3-f0c9de183eb4"],

