Cell["8.  Reinforcement learning post-training", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"61a4947a-c2cf-4640-9d66-6f98d804e3d2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "SFT teaches the model to imitate.  RL teaches it to optimise.  ",
 "After SFT, we take the model, sample completions on a task with a ",
 "verifiable reward (or a reward model), and update the policy to ",
 "make high-reward completions more likely.  Following nanochat we ",
 "use ",
 StyleBox["GRPO",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " in its simplest form: no reference model, no KL term, just ",
 "centred advantages over a group of rollouts."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8dabffe0-55e7-4c77-9946-f715d309dad4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 GraphicsBox[
  TagBox[RasterBox[CompressedData["1:"], {{0, 667.}, {1000., 0}}, {0, 255},
    ColorFunction->RGBColor,
    ImageResolution->{72, 72}],
   BoxForm`ImageTag[
   "Byte", ColorSpace -> "RGB", Interleaving -> True, 
    MetaInformation -> <|
     "Exif" -> <|
       "ImageWidth" -> 1000, "ImageLength" -> 667, "XResolution" -> 72, 
        "YResolution" -> 72, "ResolutionUnit" -> "Inch", "Software" -> 
        "Created with the Wolfram Language : www.wolfram.com", "DateTime" -> 
        DateObject[{2026, 5, 21, 15, 44, 58.}, "Instant", "Gregorian", 1.], 
        "TimeZoneOffset" -> 1|>|>],
   Selectable->False],
  DefaultBaseStyle->"ImageGraphics",
  ImageSizeRaw->{1000., 667.},
  PlotRange->{{0, 1000.}, {0, 667.}}]], "Output",
 CellMargins->{{Inherited, Inherited}, {5, 10}},
 TextAlignment->Center,
 CellLabel->"",ExpressionUUID->"6bc86b2e-323d-4abd-b5e6-a5ef2ce75693"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Figure 8.1.  One GRPO step.  Sample K rollouts from \
the policy at temperature T, score with a reward function, centre rewards to \
get advantages, take a policy-gradient step.  No value head, no KL term, no \
reference model.  The variance across the K rollouts IS the advantage signal.",
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic]], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"90feb4cd-f37a-477c-9a35-\
0576db2544a2"],

Cell["8.1  The recipe in five lines", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"4b248ad4-f333-4657-9d9a-da13ae5afc21"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "1. ",
 StyleBox["Sample.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData["K"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"fd876848-1baa-40f6-961e-a0af1548dbad"],
 " rollouts from the current policy at temperature ",
 Cell[BoxData["T"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"d28a4f5a-b3a2-47b3-bfeb-c057e998fe98"],
 ".\n",
 "2. ",
 StyleBox["Score.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " Each rollout gets a reward (binary for verifiable tasks).\n",
 "3. ",
 StyleBox["Centre.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"advantages", 
   RowBox[{" ", 
    RowBox[{"=", " "}]}], "rewards", 
   RowBox[{" ", 
    RowBox[{"-", " "}]}], 
   RowBox[{"mean", 
    RowBox[{"(", "rewards", ")"}]}]}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"e26663b6-3897-4243-b987-6bfc2d75da3d"],
 ".  No z-score normalisation (per DAPO).\n",
 "4. ",
 StyleBox["Compute.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " Policy-gradient loss ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"L", 
   RowBox[{" ", 
    RowBox[{"=", " "}]}], "-", "\[Sum]"}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"8cc428a1-a714-4d47-96d3-f68fb6f0ec34"],
 "  advantage_i * log p_\[Theta](rollout_i).\n",
 "5. ",
 StyleBox["Step.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " ADAM on L."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bdb8197a-ab77-41e9-a61d-29be2a5426f2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "What is deliberately absent: no reference model, no KL ",
 "divergence, no value head, no importance weighting.  The reward ",
 StyleBox["is",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " the ground truth; the variance across the ",
 Cell[BoxData["K"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"2bdfadfd-3ff5-49e0-bc3e-5951dbadc496"],
 " rollouts ",
 StyleBox["is",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " the advantage signal.  It is shocking how simple this is once you ",
 "accept that you don't need PPO's machinery for tasks with ",
 "verifiable correctness."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e3cdda0e-957d-4e6d-81aa-5c96a1f8732d"],

Cell["8.2  The toy verifiable task", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"dbe2a60a-ff7d-4149-8cd9-1eaf9402b710"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For the educational demo we use the trivial task ",
 "\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]end your continuation with the ",
 StyleBox["<|eot|>",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " token within k tokens.\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]  Binary reward: ",
 "1.0 if the rollout contains ",
 StyleBox["<|eot|>",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", else 0.0.  Small models post-trained from random init learn to ",
 "do this in a few minutes of CPU time, while preserving all the ",
 "GRPO bookkeeping that scales to real verifiable tasks (GSM8K, ",
 "code, format-following)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1ce9d7fe-c687-49c3-b157-8162ce548a8c"],

Cell["9.  An interactive chat widget", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"cb9c4b77-59f9-4ab1-95b2-a7ddde37efae"],

Cell["\<\
We close with the artefact every reader actually wants: a chat interface, \
inside the notebook, talking to the model we just built.  An input field, a \
transcript pane, a streaming generator.  Drop the widget cell into a \
notebook, evaluate, type, get a reply.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5875312b-ec4f-4e2b-9ff6-fa632b56bdb7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The widget is a ",
 StyleBox["DynamicModule",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " holding a running transcript, an input field, and Send/Reset ",
 "buttons.  Each Send triggers ",
 StyleBox["chatTurn",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", which formats the existing transcript and the new user message ",
 "in the chat template, runs the model autoregressively until ",
 StyleBox["<|eot|>",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " or the max-tokens limit, and appends the assistant turn.  A ",
 "screenshot of what the widget looks like in action:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2e3767ca-2758-4c5a-8904-862319ce13c8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 GraphicsBox[
  TagBox[RasterBox[CompressedData["1:"], {{0, 174.46153846153845`}, {553.8461538461538, 0}}, {0, 255},
    ColorFunction->RGBColor,
    ImageResolution->{130, 130}],
   BoxForm`ImageTag[
   "Byte", ColorSpace -> "RGB", Interleaving -> True, 
    MetaInformation -> <|
     "Exif" -> <|
       "ImageWidth" -> 1000, "ImageLength" -> 315, "XResolution" -> 130, 
        "YResolution" -> 130, "ResolutionUnit" -> "Inch", "Software" -> 
        "Created with the Wolfram Language : www.wolfram.com", "DateTime" -> 
        DateObject[{2026, 5, 21, 15, 44, 58.}, "Instant", "Gregorian", 1.], 
        "TimeZoneOffset" -> 1|>|>],
   Selectable->False],
  DefaultBaseStyle->"ImageGraphics",
  ImageSizeRaw->{553.8461538461538, 174.46153846153845`},
  PlotRange->{{0, 553.8461538461538}, {0, 174.46153846153845`}}]], "Output",
 CellMargins->{{Inherited, Inherited}, {5, 10}},
 TextAlignment->Center,
 CellLabel->"",ExpressionUUID->"52dcf537-73f8-4ec8-a818-ef03379a20c5"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Figure 9.1.  Static snapshot of the in-notebook chat \
widget.  The transcript at top accumulates turns; the input field and \
Send/Reset buttons drive new requests.  Evaluate the cell below in Wolfram \
Desktop to interact with the real version (requires a loaded SFT checkpoint).",
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic]], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"68745abc-a547-4d7a-a49e-\
a2748eeec847"],

Cell["\<\
(* The chat widget.  Open this notebook in Wolfram Desktop and
   evaluate to interact. *)
If[ValueQ[sftNet],
  LLMAtoZ`Chat`chatWidget[sftNet,
    bpe[\"MergeRules\"], tokId,
    AssociationThread[Range[Length[vocab]] -> vocab],
    \"MaxNew\" -> 60, \"Temperature\" -> 0.8, \"TopK\" -> 40],
  Style[\"SFT checkpoint not loaded; run Path A first.\", Red]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"7b0fe4ca-64be-43b0-a81d-d0371c23f51f"],

Cell["\<\
The model is small and undertrained for the scale of natural language; it \
will not pass a Turing test.  But the entire pipeline from BPE tokenisation \
through GRPO post-training is something you wrote (and could change).  That \
is the point of this notebook.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a951d1d4-1e38-40d1-b450-40a7c2f8d779"],

Cell["\<\
10.  Scaling up: from 20 toy pairs to 20,000 Alpaca instructions\
\>", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"e0b9e8e9-c372-42b1-a550-ef38ac6d676e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 GraphicsBox[
  TagBox[RasterBox[CompressedData["1:"], {{0, 1000.}, {1000., 0}}, {0, 255},
    ColorFunction->RGBColor,
    ImageResolution->{72, 72}],
   BoxForm`ImageTag[
