Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Figure 10.0.  The plot of this chapter: same \
pipeline, but the toy SFT corpus of 20 hand-written Q&A pairs (Chapter 7) is \
replaced by 20,000 instruction\[Dash]response pairs from Alpaca-cleaned, and \
the 124M small base is replaced by the 355M medium.  Two knobs, \
simultaneously.",
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic]], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"65088d72-7ffc-4c35-bca1-\
4fef41ebb980"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The chat widget above works \[LongDash] but the answers are obviously ",
 "wrong (\"Hamlet is a playwright who wrote the play in 1763\").  The ",
 "model from Chapter 7 was fine-tuned on twenty hand-written Q&A pairs.  ",
 "It learned the ",
 StyleBox["template",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " (User: \[Ellipsis] Assistant: \[Ellipsis]) but no real content.  ",
 "If we want a model that ",
 StyleBox["actually",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " gives sensible answers, we need to pull two levers at once: a ",
 "bigger base model, and a much bigger SFT dataset."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bf17f6c9-bb75-4288-a4aa-6184938a573c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This chapter documents the actual run we did to find out what each ",
 "lever buys us.  Same pipeline; we just feed it more.  Code is in ",
 StyleBox["discussion-model/src/",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " of the repo, separate from the per-part notebooks so you can run it ",
 "without disturbing the rest of the series."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6c3baee4-208c-4927-89b8-a6e021b97e91"],

Cell["10.1  The plan, and what we ended up doing", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"46a77bf1-0a83-409d-87f5-4cb84e84f4cc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Three knobs.  ",
 StyleBox["Base model",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " (GPT-2 small, medium, large \[LongDash] 124M / 355M / 774M ",
 "params).  ",
 StyleBox["Dataset",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " (toy 20 pairs \[Rule] Alpaca-cleaned, 51,760 instructions, Apache ",
 "2.0).  ",
 StyleBox["Compute",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " (Mac mini CPU \[Rule] Wolfram Cloud GPU via ",
 StyleBox["RemoteBatchSubmit",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ")."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"49810a30-6224-41ea-9eb3-5a885c7ff926"],

Cell["What worked, what didn't:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e56df5cc-1933-431f-8480-b84aa1c53f24"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\[Bullet] ",
 StyleBox["GPT-2 small (124M) SFT on 10k Alpaca, Mac mini CPU, 3 ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 StyleBox["epochs",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 ".  Died of an unrelated ",
 "license check at 2h26m, mid-epoch 2.  Epoch-1 ",
 "checkpoint survives.\n",
 "\[Bullet] ",
 StyleBox["GPT-2 medium (355M) SFT on full Alpaca, cloud GPU1xL40S, 1 ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 StyleBox["epoch",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 ".  Out-of-memory at 37k of 51,760 ",
 "examples.  Cause: our own ",
 StyleBox["TrainingProgressFunction",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " periodically saving a ",
 StyleBox["NetTake",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " copy to a ",
 StyleBox["CloudObject",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " leaked 1.4 GB per checkpoint.  \[Sterling]5.48 burnt.\n",
 "\[Bullet] ",
 StyleBox["GPT-2 medium SFT on 20k Alpaca, cloud GPU4xL4, 1 epoch ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "\[Dash] same code with the periodic checkpoint removed.  ",
 StyleBox["Succeeded.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "  53.6 min wall, final loss 1.367.  \[Sterling]12.75.  This is our ",
 "production discussion model.\n",
 "\[Bullet] ",
 StyleBox["GPT-2 large (774M) SFT on 10k Alpaca, two attempts on ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 StyleBox["GPU4xL4",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 ".  Both got within ",
 "one batch (>99.9%) of finishing the epoch, then OOM\[CloseCurlyQuote]d ",
 "on the post-training ",
 StyleBox["CloudPut",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " cascade: 3 GB net + ",
 StyleBox["NetTake",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " copy + serialization buffer > 24 GiB single-GPU memory.  ",
 "\[Sterling]25.46 burnt.  Lesson banked, large shelved."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"267894a0-ec3f-48ec-9d79-bbfce753cdb1"],

Cell["\<\
Total spend: about \[Sterling]45 (\[TildeTilde] $56) across the cloud runs.  \
Time: a working day from \"can we even submit a GPU job\" to \"the model says \
'The capital of France is Paris.'\"  The educational point isn't the dollar \
figure; it's that the bugs you hit at this scale are not the bugs you hit on \
Mac-mini-sized toy runs.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"770e6a4f-90e5-4149-9946-cd02c87bd6ca"],

Cell["10.2  The dataset: Alpaca-cleaned", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"64da5eae-3e7b-4137-a8a5-d6afe51237b4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Alpaca-cleaned is the Stanford ",
 StyleBox["Alpaca",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " dataset (Taori et al. 2023) after a community cleanup by ",
 StyleBox["yahma",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " on HuggingFace.  51,760 instruction\[Dash]response pairs in three ",
 "fields: ",
 StyleBox["instruction",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["input",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " (optional context), ",
 StyleBox["output",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ".  Apache 2.0.  44 MB on ",
 "disk."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"98f1c88a-1c1e-4aea-80cd-ab1c3262fdd6"],

Cell["\<\
(* Fetch + look at one example. *)
example = First @ LLMAtoZ`Discussion`loadAlpacaExamples[1];
example\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"3904c9d4-9aa6-4980-bdec-7208362e2ad1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 GraphicsBox[
  TagBox[RasterBox[CompressedData["1:"], {{0, 224.64}, {720., 0}}, {0, 255},
    ColorFunction->RGBColor,
    ImageResolution->{100, 100}],
   BoxForm`ImageTag[
   "Byte", ColorSpace -> "RGB", Interleaving -> True, 
    MetaInformation -> <|
     "Exif" -> <|
       "ImageWidth" -> 1000, "ImageLength" -> 312, "XResolution" -> 100, 
        "YResolution" -> 100, "ResolutionUnit" -> "Inch", "Software" -> 
        "Created with the Wolfram Language : www.wolfram.com", "DateTime" -> 
        DateObject[{2026, 5, 21, 15, 44, 58.}, "Instant", "Gregorian", 1.], 
        "TimeZoneOffset" -> 1|>|>],
   Selectable->False],
  DefaultBaseStyle->"ImageGraphics",
  ImageSizeRaw->{720., 224.64},
  PlotRange->{{0, 720.}, {0, 224.64}}]], "Output",
 CellMargins->{{Inherited, Inherited}, {5, 10}},
 TextAlignment->Center,
 CellLabel->"",ExpressionUUID->"f7f500c2-fb37-44f6-b724-d33b01e124d9"],

Cell["\<\
Format each row as plain text with markers GPT-2's BPE already tokenises \
naturally:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1729559f-6490-4cb4-b9e5-697895a381c7"],

Cell["LLMAtoZ`Discussion`formatPair[example]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"0bed722f-a6b2-4f68-bf19-dddc860a37af"],

Cell["\<\
User: Give three tips for staying healthy.
Assistant: 1. Eat a balanced and nutritious diet: Make sure your meals are \
inclusive of a variety of fruits and vegetables, lean protein, whole grains, \
and healthy fats. This helps to provide your body with the essential \
nutrients to function at its best and can help prevent chronic diseases.

2. Engage in regular physical activity: Exercise is crucial for maintaining \
strong bones, muscles, and cardiovascular health. Aim for at least 150 \
minutes of moderate aerobic exercise or 75 minutes of vigorous exercise each \
week.

3. Get enough sleep: Getting enough quality sleep is crucial for physical and \
mental well-being. It helps to regulate mood, improve cognitive function, and \
supports healthy growth and immune function. Aim for 7-9 hours of sleep each \
night.
\
\>", "Output",
 FontFamily->"Courier",
 FontSize->12,
 CellLabel->"Out= ",ExpressionUUID->"69780f2d-2620-4652-943d-62d909502b01"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Why plain text and not the ",
 StyleBox["<|user|>...<|assistant|>...<|eot|>",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " template from Chapter 7?  Because extending GPT-2's tied input/output ",
 "embedding to add three new tokens is fiddly (we tried; it broke ",
 "NetTrain's autograd in a way we didn't want to spend more credits ",
 "debugging).  Plain text keeps the 50,257-entry vocabulary intact and ",
 "the weight tying alive.  The price: no learned end-of-turn signal, so ",
 "the trained model sometimes babbles past the answer (see 10.5)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"81111025-9ee5-4ab4-b8ca-0e7a6bc6f30f"],

Cell["10.3  Surgery on the pretrained NetModel", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"1d6b0150-ad8c-4191-b4b5-eace0c1d69ec"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The unmodified ",
 StyleBox["NetModel",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " for GPT-2 small / medium / large is wired for ",
 StyleBox["inference",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ": a long prompt in, one next-token distribution out.  Its tail is ",
 StyleBox["SequenceLastLayer",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " \[Rule] ",
 StyleBox["LinearLayer[vocab]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " \[Rule] ",
 StyleBox["SoftmaxLayer",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ".  For training we need per-position logits at every step.  Three ",
 "changes, in three lines:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bdc3b9fc-c5fe-4cda-938a-43ed695827d4"],

Cell["\<\
(* Pull the pretrained net, drop the inference tail, wrap the
   per-position classifier with NetMapOperator so it applies row-wise. *)
gpt = NetModel[{
  \"GPT-2 Transformer Trained on WebText Data\",
  \"Size\" -> \"345M\", \"Task\" -> \"LanguageModeling\"}];
trunk = NetChain[{
  NetExtract[gpt, \"embedding\"],
  NetExtract[gpt, \"decoder\"],
  NetMapOperator[NetExtract[gpt, \"classifier\"]]}];
Information[trunk, \"ArraysTotalElementCount\"]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"b28883b3-91f8-49a2-9a7e-465e8628ecaa"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Same 354,823,168 parameters as before.  The classifier's ",
 StyleBox["SharedArrays",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " linkage to the token embedding stays intact; we don't have to ",
 "re-tie it manually.  This trunk is what we train."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d9a2d853-d2cb-4497-b685-7df530d19cde"],

Cell["\<\
10.4  RemoteBatchSubmit: code that runs on someone else's GPU\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"d66f6d7e-2696-42c4-9274-fe9f40dce729"],

Cell[BoxData[
 GraphicsBox[
  TagBox[RasterBox[CompressedData["1:"], {{0, 1000.}, {1000., 0}}, {0, 255},
    ColorFunction->RGBColor,
    ImageResolution->{72, 72}],
   BoxForm`ImageTag[
   "Byte", ColorSpace -> "RGB", Interleaving -> True, 
    MetaInformation -> <|
     "Exif" -> <|
       "ImageWidth" -> 1000, "ImageLength" -> 1000, "XResolution" -> 72, 
        "YResolution" -> 72, "ResolutionUnit" -> "Inch", "Software" -> 
        "Created with the Wolfram Language : www.wolfram.com", "DateTime" -> 
        DateObject[{2026, 5, 21, 15, 44, 58.}, "Instant", "Gregorian", 1.], 
        "TimeZoneOffset" -> 1|>|>],
   Selectable->False],
  DefaultBaseStyle->"ImageGraphics",
  ImageSizeRaw->{1000., 1000.},
  PlotRange->{{0, 1000.}, {0, 1000.}}]], "Output",
 CellMargins->{{Inherited, Inherited}, {5, 10}},
 TextAlignment->Center,
 CellLabel->"",ExpressionUUID->"f3ec59d1-791d-492c-b32c-e97c2a4eb60e"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Figure 10.1.  RemoteBatchSubmit conceptually: we send \
the training expression up to the Wolfram Cloud, it lands on a GPU machine \
somewhere (an L4 or L40S), runs there, and we get the trained net back on \
disk.  The Mac mini at the bottom stays at idle.",
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic]], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"383a4bcf-7bda-4510-be63-\
bfacdc942a3e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Mac mini CPU can SFT GPT-2 small overnight.  Anything bigger needs ",
 "a GPU.  Wolfram Cloud's batch system exposes one through ",
 StyleBox["RemoteBatchSubmit",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ".  The pattern:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f6e9f4fa-eb96-44a7-95b3-9027d82d413a"],

Cell["\<\
(* Build an environment that targets a specific machine class. *)
env = RemoteBatchSubmissionEnvironment[\"WolframBatch\",
  <|\"RemoteMachineClass\" -> \"GPU1xL40S\"|>];
(* Available classes on this account include:
     Basic1x8       -- default CPU box, very cheap
     Basic4x16      -- bigger CPU
     GPU1xL40S      -- 1x NVIDIA L40S, 44 GiB VRAM, ~1120 credits/hr
     GPU4xL4        -- 4x NVIDIA L4, 89 GiB total, ~2765 credits/hr
   ~200 credits per pound sterling. *)\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"b4fd8a8b-c274-4779-9b14-03628eca1608"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "And then submit a piece of WL code that runs out there.  ",
 StyleBox["Critical gotcha",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 ": ",
 StyleBox["RemoteBatchSubmit",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " holds its second argument internally.  An explicit ",
 StyleBox["Hold[\[Ellipsis]]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " wrapper around the Module ",
 StyleBox["survives",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " to the remote, where evaluating ",
 StyleBox["Hold[Module[\[Ellipsis]]]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " just returns the Hold itself \[LongDash] the Module never runs.  ",
 "Pass the Module bare:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c947c555-47de-4440-924b-2ec154c01c9d"],

Cell["\<\
(* CORRECT *)
(* job = RemoteBatchSubmit[env, Module[{out = <||>, ...}, ...; out]]; *)
(* WRONG -- the Module never evaluates remotely *)
(* job = RemoteBatchSubmit[env, Hold[Module[...]]]; *)\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"c1aebb17-ebce-401b-8f4b-e2669e7768bc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We learnt this by burning \[Sterling]0.27 on a no-op job that ",
 "looked successful but had no Result.  Documented at length in ",
 StyleBox["discussion-model/src/submit_gpu_prod.wls",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a06b1ac7-e3c3-41d0-982a-162f9ab1f813"],

Cell["10.5  What the trained medium model actually says", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"cea838d5-1b99-4967-8d88-4b20a771ed44"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "After the successful 20k-Alpaca, 1-epoch run on GPU4xL4, the saved ",
 "stripped net lives at ",
 StyleBox["discussion-model/data/discussion_medium_20k.wlnet",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " (1.35 GB, gitignored; the CloudObject URL is in the run summary).  ",
 "Compare its answers to the Chapter 7 toy SFT model:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b9413b3f-ba34-40bd-ba0c-e0d1464a2f4b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Sample generations from the Alpaca-trained medium (",
 StyleBox["T = 0.7, top-k = 40",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "):"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a5fb7041-2e54-41a6-a1c0-d9ba26da7c6f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["User:",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " What is the capital of France?\n",
 StyleBox["Assistant:",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " The capital of France is Paris."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cac211cb-580e-4d58-b8d8-4715a900b3ae"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["User:",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " Give three tips for staying healthy.\n",
 StyleBox["Assistant:",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " 1. Eat a balanced and nutritious diet: A healthy diet can help to ",
 "maintain good health by providing the necessary vitamins, minerals, ",
 "and fiber to support good heart health and mental wellbeing\[Ellipsis] ",
 "2. Get enough sleep\[Ellipsis]"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"42a58691-e03f-41d6-80ab-0d36613baa13"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["User:",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " Recommend a book to read.\n",
 StyleBox["Assistant:",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " One great book to read is \"To Kill a Mockingbird\" by Harper Lee. ",
 "This novel is a classic that teaches the importance of empathy, the ",
 "power of a good deed, and the true worth of one's choices."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"acf3bfc1-c0bf-4aa1-8df0-c18ac39ee580"],

Cell["Compare to Chapter 7's toy SFT for the same prompts:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a619beb2-bfeb-45da-a07a-cac0658b5ad3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["User:",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " Who wrote Hamlet?\n",
 StyleBox["Assistant",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 StyleBox[" (toy SFT, Chapter 7)",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ": Hamlet is ",
 "a playwright who wrote the play in 1763.\n",
 StyleBox["Assistant",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 StyleBox[" (Alpaca SFT, this chapter)",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ": Shakespeare was a Roman Catholic poet, dramatist, and playwright ",
 "from about 586 to 1140."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ef01ce47-d76b-49ab-a57e-07c71d08bdfd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Both are wrong on dates.  The Alpaca model is right on ",
 StyleBox["author and role",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " (\"poet, dramatist, and playwright\") in a way the toy SFT isn't.  ",
 "It is also obviously not GPT-4.  This is roughly what 355M parameters ",
 "and a 20k-instruction SFT buys: chat fluency and rough fact recall, ",
 "with regular errors in dates, names, and reasoning chains.  Bigger ",
 "base + more data + RL would push each of those metrics."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a8416f57-86aa-4408-9096-09415166b29b"],

Cell["10.6  Why we can't (easily) train GPT-2 medium on the Mac", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"517bbaa8-83c8-4c1e-b7ee-f5ab88fdb0dc"],

Cell[BoxData[
 GraphicsBox[
  TagBox[RasterBox[CompressedData["1:"], {{0, 1000.}, {1000., 0}}, {0, 255},
    ColorFunction->RGBColor,
    ImageResolution->{72, 72}],
   BoxForm`ImageTag[
   "Byte", ColorSpace -> "RGB", Interleaving -> True, 
    MetaInformation -> <|
     "Exif" -> <|
       "ImageWidth" -> 1000, "ImageLength" -> 1000, "XResolution" -> 72, 
        "YResolution" -> 72, "ResolutionUnit" -> "Inch", "Software" -> 
        "Created with the Wolfram Language : www.wolfram.com", "DateTime" -> 
        DateObject[{2026, 5, 21, 15, 44, 59.}, "Instant", "Gregorian", 1.], 
        "TimeZoneOffset" -> 1|>|>],
   Selectable->False],
  DefaultBaseStyle->"ImageGraphics",
  ImageSizeRaw->{1000., 1000.},
  PlotRange->{{0, 1000.}, {0, 1000.}}]], "Output",
 CellMargins->{{Inherited, Inherited}, {5, 10}},
 TextAlignment->Center,
 CellLabel->"",ExpressionUUID->"7d67331b-fdb8-4f35-8f16-7d3ff2b8a5b2"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Figure 10.2.  Out-of-memory: trying to save a 3 GB \
GPT-2 large checkpoint on a 24 GiB single-GPU L4 after training fills the \
device.  Training itself succeeded; the post-training NetTake + CloudPut \
cascade did not.  Twice.",
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic]], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2eb1246d-42be-4d4c-a174-\
94ae6ed0b4b8"],

Cell["\<\
The same surgery code that works on GPT-2 small (124M) hits a specific \
low-level bug on GPT-2 medium when run on Mac CPU.  The error is at the MXNet \
operator level:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"de9b2e74-8c8b-42ed-a868-9e3f71b86d17"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["MXNetError: Check failed: assign(&dattr, vec.at(i)): \n",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 StyleBox["Incompatible attr in node _copyto at 0-th output: \n",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 StyleBox["expected [4096], got [1024]\n",
  FontFamily->"Courier"]
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e94323d9-a0cd-4225-b915-7400d80b56ea"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The numbers 1024 and 4096 are GPT-2 medium's ",
 StyleBox["d_model",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["d_ff",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ".  Something in the gradient routing across our reconstructed chain ",
 "gets confused at this exact size.  Same code, same call, works ",
 "perfectly on cuDNN (cloud GPU) and on MXNet-CPU at small.  Not ",
 "fixable from the application layer.  Practical implication: ",
 "anything bigger than small needs the cloud."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4f0d5361-9635-4488-9e59-8f7decc39f83"],

Cell["10.7  Inference is slow in Wolfram Language on Mac", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"045e0bd0-5ebb-4fce-b91a-c6ad8970e983"],

Cell[BoxData[
